    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="1231" n="1191" xml:id="pg1191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">782.5 MSP/12–2851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Turkey
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d681-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-28T19:20:00-05:00">December 28,
                            1951—7:20 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>560. We will accept and urge you make strong effort obtain Turk acceptance fol
                    wording as substitute (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) last para Deptel 552 Dec
                        26<anchor n="2" xml:id="d681-f2"/> “No conversions into other currencies
                    will occur without taking the Turk foreign exchange position into acct nor will
                    they be made except pursuant to mutually satisfactory arrangements”. (Embtel 578
                    Dec 28.)</p>
                <p>As last resort and if you believe deadlock wld otherwise result you may add “to
                    be agreed upon” following “satisfactory arrangements”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d681-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d681-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Lincoln and Moore, GTI, and cleared with Morse, ECA, and Gray,
                    L/E.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d681-f2" n="2" xml:id="d681-f2-content">
